sntrup761 0.4.0, https://github.com/mikelodder7/sntrup761
Crates.io archive SHA256: a7fadfbd0a7d18ce7b04ed753c018a3e5d2ac2b3603f70507cd84012e76fa8a8
Licenses and original manifest retained.

Local changes:
- Cargo manifest disables dependency default features (rand, rand_chacha,
  thiserror, sha2, subtle, zeroize) for allocation-free bare-metal RV32.
- workspace.rs adds caller-owned scalar reciprocal, product, sampling and
  encoding scratch. r3.rs, rq.rs, rq/encoding.rs, zx.rs and utils.rs borrow
  those buffers instead of allocating them on the call stack.
- lib.rs adds *_with_workspace entry points. Existing entry points retain
  their signatures and allocate temporary scratch. Workspace APIs erase
  scratch before return; Workspace also zeroizes on drop.

Polynomial arithmetic, sampling, serialization, hashing and implicit rejection
are unchanged. rvaccel tests check 16 seeded transcript hashes generated from
untouched upstream 0.4.0, alongside independent IETF decapsulation vectors.
